WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.280
You did it! We made a comeback!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.650
How is it, Shigeno? Will you be able to pitch another inning?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.160
Of course!

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.830
I originally pitched full games, after all. {Pitching the entire game from start to finish, in case that was wierdly worded}

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.580
No matter what inning or what game it is,  I'm always ready to pitch!

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.290
<i>Just you wait, Junior!</i>

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.300
<i>I'll definitely strike you out!</i>

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.510
Strike out!

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.720
The game is over!

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.640
The Bats made an amazing comeback and won the first game!

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.020
But what incredible pitching Goro Shigeno displayed!

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.980
Out of nine outs, eight were strikeouts!

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.230
<i>I see.</i>

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.700
<i>Who'd have imagined that he would transfer to Memphis?</i>

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.490
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.870
<i>This time for sure, I will stop your breath. {Or "kill", but not in the meaning of actually killing him, rather to "kill" him out of baseball :P}</i>

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.930
It's the semifinal of the playoffs.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.690
In this game between the Bats and the Sharks,

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.940
the Bats are leading as we enter the top of the 9th inning!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.650
And on the mound stands Shigeno!

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.570
Will he be able to suppress the last batter?

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.660
We're counting on you, Shigeno!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.450
Just one more.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.620
Just take out one more and we'll advance to the finals!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.840
Come!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.880
Shigeno!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.340
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.260
Strike!

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.220
Strike!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.400
Strike out!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.310
Game over!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.360
Oh yeah!

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.570
The game is over!

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.990
The Bats defeat the Sharks with 3 wins and 2 losses!

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:50.620
They advance to the finals of the playoffs!

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.210
The Bats' leading star is Shigeno, who's been a great closer in every winning game. {Not sure about the term "relief" in baseball... but I believe what he means is that Shigeno has switched in in every winning match and been a good pitcher in finishing up the game.} {yaHzee: wasn't sure about relief, but I'm guessing that it's referring to him being the closer.}

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.670
He was the motivating power that carried the Bats to the finals!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.680
<i>And so...</i>

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.140
<i>We, the Bats,</i>

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.810
<i>went to the battlefield where we would play against...</i>

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.770
<i>the Oklahoma Falcons, which also won their semifinal.</i>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.930
<i>So that's how it was.</i>

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.090
<i>So you...</i>

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.350
<i>were that dead idiot's son.</i>

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.270
<i>What was that?</i>

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.980
<i>What did you say just now!?</i>

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.810
<i>Try and say it again!</i>

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.480
<i>I'll say it as many times as you'd like.</i>

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.030
<i>Who would've thought that the son of the idiotic player who died from having a bean ball hit his head,</i>

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.400
<i>would come to America to play baseball?</i>

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.830
<i>It's no wonder I can't feel an ounce of talent in you, you third-rate pitcher.</i>

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:15.920
<i>Hurry up, return to Japan, and die playing pretend baseball, just like your father.</i>

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.880
<i>I'll kill you!{i have no damn idea what's up here, this shows late whatever I do; watch it softsubbed, or retime it (it IS timed properly..-sangofe}</i>

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.800
<i>I won't forgive you...</i>

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.390
<i>for making fun of my dad!</i>

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.470
<i>That's for sure!</i>

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.270
What's the matter, Shigeno?

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.980
It's nothing.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.570
Rather than worrying about me, you should take this chance and rest your body, old man.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.910
<i>Gibson Jr.</i>

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.920
The semifinal of the playoffs between the Bats and the Sharks was a never-ending pitcher's duel.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.970
However, taking the plate in the 8th inning, Shigeno,

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:14.600
pitching for two innings once again, struck out four players and showed excellent pitching overall: a true winning pitcher.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.640
The Memphis Bats advance to the finals.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.940
Continuing on, the next semifinal in the playoffs-

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.240
Where are you going, Joe?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.670
<i>Honda Jr, huh?</i>

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>To think he'd be Memphis' closer...</i>

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.100
<i>Interesting!</i>

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:59.230
<i>The suffering I've had to go through that began on that day 12 years ago...</i>

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:01.810
<i>I'll let you feel it too!</i>

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.020
<i>Those hellish days!</i>

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.070
That day...

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.610
as dad was playing in Japan...

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:14.620
Honda Shigeharu died at my dad's hand because he couldn't dodge the dead ball.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.040
<i>Give him back!</i>

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.750
<i>Give my daddy...</i>

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.800
<i>back!</i>

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:30.630
Sorry, boy.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.100
Papa...

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.900
Get out of my sight!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.820
Dear.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.990
That was an accident.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.450
You don't have to act that way...

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.990
Shut up!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:06.340
I did something to Honda and his son that I can't undo.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.510
I'll stay in Japan.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:22.440
For the sake of the Japanese fans who've lost the great player Honda Shigeharu.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.060
I want to fill that hole as best as I can.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.920
Strike out!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.000
Gibson strikes out three players right off the bat!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.420
What a wonderful start of the game the starting pitcher, Gibson, has made!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.600
What kind of play will he show today? {Hard to hear this one, since Junior is talking in the foreground, but should be something like this, probably}

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.220
Okay, you're doing great, Papa!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.600
Do your best!

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.230
What's the matter, Mama?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.270
Aren't you going to cheer for Papa?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.780
Dear...

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.160
Please.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.950
Let's return home to America.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.410
I can't do that.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.660
Please think a little bit about the children as well!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.920
I'm sorry.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.290
I have to pitch here in Japan.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.880
For the Japanese fans...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.800
and for Honda Jr. as well.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.090
Why must you...

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.470
go so far?

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.060
There, there.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.280
What are you doing?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.700
Your dad killed someone, right?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.700
What!?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.740
Help! Murderer!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:01.830
You're wrong!

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.950
Papa isn't a murderer!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.890
<i>You're wrong!</i>

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.140
<i>Papa isn't a murderer!</i>

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:25.770
<i>He's not...!</i>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.600
Don't badmouth my papa!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.600
Don't badmouth my papa!

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.900
<i>And then...</i>

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.950
<i>because of the Honda father and son,</i>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.910
<i>our family was...</i>

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.620
Divorce?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.660
What's a divorce?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.330
It means that Papa and Mama will live in different places.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.540
We won't be a family anymore.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.630
You and I will stay in Japan,

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.840
and Mama and Melissa will return home to America.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:02.510
No!

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.720
I don't like that!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:05.890
That's strange!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.390
Why do we all have to be separated?

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:10.310
Why!?

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.190
Mama can't get used to the Japanese lifestyle...

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:15.980
She tried her best, but...

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.200
there were a lot of things we didn't agree on.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.870
Then Papa just has to return to America, right?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.740
You can play baseball in America and things'll work out, right?

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.290
I can't do that.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.250
Papa has...

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:35.250
Papa has to atone for the sin that my mistake has caused here in Japan.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.890
Why?

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:50.350
Does Papa think the Hondas are more important than his family?

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.070
Mama...

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.190
Melissa...

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.240
<i>In the end, Dad chose...</i>

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.280
<i>to continue playing baseball in Japan.</i>

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.950
<i>Our family became separated...</i>

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.120
<i>And then...</i>

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.340
<i>My mother and Melissa,</i>

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:19.130
<i>who had returned to America,</i>

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.760
<i>died in an accident.</i>

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.680
Come.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:27.970
Junior.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.430
Put your flowers here too.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.230
Junior.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:33.600
It's your fault...

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.150
The ones who killed Mama and Melissa...

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.570
were you and Honda! {Kohn: Or more literally, it's "The ones who killed mama and Melissa... was you and Honda!" Whichever gives the best dramatic effect.}

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.330
<i>Since then... I've not spoken with my dad again.</i>

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>And then...</i>

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.250
<i>The day after that Major All Star Game,</i>

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.590
<i>I enlisted in the Little League and earnestly devoted myself to baseball.</i>

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.130
<i>To crush my dad...</i>

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:11.890
<i>with the very baseball he loves!</i>

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.310
<i>Just a little more.</i>

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.600
<i>Just a little bit.</i>

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:23.360
<i>I'll knock out Honda Jr. and rise to the Majors!</i>

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.360
<i>And then...</i>

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.240
<i>I'll crush my dad!</i>

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.700
This is a free fansub.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.700
Not for sale or rent.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:07.320
It's like they're all changed people now. They're so pumped up!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.030
I'm getting a really good feeling from this.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:13.080
That's natural. Winning the League Championship is right before our eyes!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.040
Well, just watch.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:21.500
We'll show you the greatest show!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:25.670
Hey!

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.010
Garrett!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.680
Get into the batter's box!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.890
I'll work you really hard!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.000
<i>Just having a strong batter like Gibson Jr. as his opponent...</i>

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.460
<i>makes him this pumped up.</i>

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.380
Thanks for your efforts.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.720
Tomorrow, our battle against the Falcons will finally begin.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:17.270
The mass media wrote that the Falcons will be the sure champions, but we won't let them win that easily! {I'm not actually too sure what is being said at the last part, so I just put in "win" as an assumption. ~yaHzee}

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:21.310
Show those who underestimate us the spirit of the Bats!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.310
Yeah!

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.580
Mister Shigeno.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.500
Can I get your autograph?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:43.710
Autograph?

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.800
Okay, okay! No problem!

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:53.930
I'm happy! I didn't know that I have fans in Oklahoma as well...

00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:00.480
"Idiot! Who would want your autograph!?"

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.270
What's your problem, you bastard!? {ambient: timing adjustment needed}

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.480
Making a fool of someone like that!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.150
Don't screw with me!

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.440
Why you... What are you laughing at!?

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.360
No, rather, don't laugh!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.070
I'm surprised, Shigeno.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.910
You've really improved at speaking English, haven't you?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.000
Who?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.710
Geez, how cruel, to forget me.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:29.670
Who was it that saved you half a year ago when you were lost at a roadside?

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:32.340
Ginumacchi!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.890
Wow, it's really been a long time!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.720
That hurts! Stop it!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.270
How have you been?

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.270
Hey, Shigeno!

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.020
We're leaving!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:43.850
Sorry.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.230
You guys leave first.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.190
I'll be back soon.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.320
You're amazing, Shigeno.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.990
I was surprised when I heard that the Salmons released you, but...

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:01.620
now you're the Bats' closer and a step away from the Majors! {"right in front" as in almost getting there}

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.000
Well, I guess.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:09.130
Well, it's been a bit tough getting here, but I've managed somehow.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.670
I see.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.300
Anyway, what's up?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.010
Why are you here in Oklahoma, Ginumacchi?

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.600
Well, that is...

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:26.520
I know that your team is going to play against the Falcons tomorrow...

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:29.900
Oh, is that it? You missed me that much?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.030
Stupid, that's not it.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.570
Is something wrong?

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.280
Well, how should I say it...

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.080
I'm just dropping by here on my way to Japan from Dallas.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.500
Ah, I see. The season's already over, after all.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.590
Of course you'd want to go home to Japan.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.760
The food here's not bad either, but...

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.220
I'd really like to eat some Japanese food periodically.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.680
Even if you've improved your English,

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.480
you're still bad at using a knife and fork.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.020
So what?

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.190
I'm getting it down at least.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.440
I'm happy that you're still the same old you.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.650
Continue to do your best in the future as well, Shigeno.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:16.950
What's this?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.570
You're being so formal, and it's creeping me out.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.790
Shigeno.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:26.620
I won't...

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.500
be coming back to America again.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:31.880
That's why...

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.590
I want you to do your best.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.050
What's the meaning of this?

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.840
Why won't you be returning to America?

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.180
I was released.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.890
It happened at the end of the season.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.690
Hey, there's no reason for you to make such a face.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:52.480
B-But...!

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.150
B-But...!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.740
It's fine.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.660
The problem was that becoming a pro isn't that easy.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:06.160
I went there without being good enough, and almost immediately after joining the Single A,{Kohn: I'm not completly sure about the first part of this line}

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.210
I reopened my old knee wound while making a fine play to home plate.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.090
Even in the games afterwards,

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:18.340
I couldn't produce the results I wanted.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.640
I swore that in this last year...

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.300
I would produce results that both my parents and I...

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.970
would be satisfied with and made this my last chance.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.730
Unfortunately,

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.600
it didn't go well.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.520
W-Wait a minute, Ginumacchi!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.820
It didn't work out because of your injury, right?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.360
If you only heal your injury,

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.240
you could still do it! You don't know for sure!

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.070
Don't give up!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:49.540
It's fine.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.250
I've struggled with this enough already.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.500
If you're a man...

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.840
you've got to know when it's time to make a decision.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.010
Thank you, Shigeno.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.100
I'm praying from the bottom of my heart that you can fulfill the dream of playing in the Majors...

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.930
that was too far away for me to reach.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.900
Gibson Jr!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:23.240
My stomach hurts!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.070
<i>He's</i>  going to the Majors?

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.200
Don't make me laugh.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.540
How could a third-rate pitcher like him go to the Majors?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:32.920
By the way...

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:35.670
You should hurry up and go back to Japan too!

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.000
What was that!?

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:38.670
Hey.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.210
We're leaving.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:39.880
Huh?

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:41.970
Y-Yeah.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:46.220
Not only a third-rate father, but also a third-rate friend.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.640
If I eat sitting next to losers,

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.560
I'll become a loser as well!

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.560
Wait up, dammit!

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:53.560
Shigeno!

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.060
Stop with this nonsense!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:00.990
What kind of grudge do you have against me that lets you make fun of my dad, and now my friend!?

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:04.360
If it wasn't just before the game, I would beat you up!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.490
I've got grudges...

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:08.990
Mountains of them.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.660
To you and your old man as well!

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:16.830
Stop it, Shigeno!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.380
Hey, Joe!

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.800
L-Let's hurry out of here!

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:22.670
<i>What's the matter...</i>

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.180
<i>with this guy?</i>

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.260
Later.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.350
Losers.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:33.680
Just you watch, idiot!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.140
Which one of us is a loser?

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.690
I'll show you which one it is with my own hands tomorrow!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.730
Oh?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.950
That's quite the confidence. {split right here}Interesting.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.990
Then how about making a bet?

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.320
A bet?

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:52.410
If you strike me out just once in this series,

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.750
then I will go to Japan...

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:57.920
and put my hands together and apologize in front of your old man's grave!

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:01.250
But in reverse...

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.380
If I hit just one home run off your pitches,

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.930
then you will get out of America immediately!

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.140
How about it?

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:13.680
With the way your mouth was running earlier,

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:15.940
you should be able to take it on.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:17.400
D-Don't do it, Shigeno!

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:19.360
D-Don't do it, Shigeno!

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:20.940
Don't let him provoke you into falling for this!

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:25.360
That sounds interesting.

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:29.410
I accept your bet, Gibson Jr!

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:15.390
The battle where we both put our pride at stake has begun!

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:16.600
Junior,

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.470
I'll make sure to strike you out...

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:20.520
and make you kneel down...

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:21.940
in front of my dad's grave!

00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:23.690
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:26.020
Stormy Opening of a Match.

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:28.530
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
